    "lineage": "README names Lenia and Quality-Diversity in the title and describes MAP-Elites and AURORA experiments; the tree vendors a modified qdax package (__version__ 0.3.0; qdax/tasks/README.md references the 'QD Benchmarks Workshop at GECCO 2022'); lenia/patterns.py entries are named 'Aquarium (self-replicating)', 'Aquarium (swarm)' etc.; isoline_variation docstring cites 'Iso+Line-DD Variation Operator [1]'. No explicit 'descends from / supersedes' statement in README. || main loop (reader, from the code): Each generation the MixingEmitter samples parent pairs from the repertoire and applies isoline_variation (iso_sigma Gaussian noise + line_sigma interpolation), each child genotype is expressed into a 128x128 Lenia world and stepped 200 times under jax.lax.scan while recording mass/center/velocity/angle stats and a cropped phenotype, fitness and descriptor are computed from the last n_keep steps (fitness set to -inf if the world went empty, hit the border, or spread), and children are added to a CVT MAP-Elites grid (main_me.py) or to an UnstructuredRepertoire that keeps the individuals most distant from fitter neighbours in the VAE latent space, which is retrained on stored phenotypes every generation and used to re-encode the whole archive (main_aurora.py)."
